{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": []}, {"id": 3, "type": "video", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n2le03ob09re2vid01", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>: To get a good grade in the programming class, we should practice the presentation we prepared about the concept of queue.<br/>", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>: Talking about the concept of queue is not very difficult. I'm sure we'll get a good grade. However, if you want to practice, I will ask you some questions. <br/>", "time": "10000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>: That sounds great. I'm ready.<br/>", "time": "20000"}, {"id": 3, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>: Can you explain to me what queue is?<br/>", "time": "23000"}, {"id": 4, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>:Well, to understand the concept of queue, we just have to imagine a list of arranged items, and the organization of these items depends on their priority. Computers often carry out different processes at the same time. However, the operating system needs to prioritize to avoid delays or errors.<br/>", "time": "27000"}, {"id": 5, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>:Excellent, now, what concepts should we take into account when we talk about queue?<br/>", "time": "49000"}, {"id": 6, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>:To be able to work with queue, it's important to take into account concepts such as FIFO which means first in, first out; buffering which refers to storing data temporarily for later use, and finally, you need to know that the name of the place where we add items is the tail or rear, and the name of the place where we remove items is the head or front.<br/>", "time": "55000"}, {"id": 7, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>:Having those concepts clear helps a lot!<br/>", "time": "83000"}, {"id": 8, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>:Now, you should close the presentation by explaining what you understood about the concept of queue.<br/>", "time": "86000"}, {"id": 9, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>:So, to sum up, I understood that a queue organizes different items by priority, and the system adds these items at the tail and removes them from the head, for this reason, we can say that there is a FIFO structure. The main purpose of a queue is organizing processes and prioritizing applications that should get the attention of the processor first. What else should we say?<br/>", "time": "93000"}, {"id": 10, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Kyle</strong>:To create a queue, the system finds a block of memory and sets up pointers, and that we can find straight queues or circular queues.<br/>", "time": "120500"}, {"id": 11, "image": "", "text": "<strong>Dave</strong>:Oh, that's right!<br/>", "time": "130000"}]}, "type": "video"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain what queue is in software programming.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about concepts related to queue and software programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand different information about the concept of queue.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Why do computers become slow?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How do computers run programs?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type":