tent": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}]}, {"id": 11, "type": "DWS", "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Let's define what a queue is.  ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": ""}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Queue", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about programming.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations. Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Connectors for Contrast and Addition: For This Reason and However", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are different tools we can use to improve our writing skills, for example, the connectors \u201cfor this reason\u201d and \u201chowever\u201d.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Computers often carry out different processes at the same time. However, the operating system needs to prioritize to avoid delays or errors. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I understood that a queue organizes different items by priority, and the systems adds these items at the tail and removes them from the head, for this reason, we can say that there is a FIFO structure.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The connector <span class=\"strong\">for this reason </span> explains the cause of something. First, you give the explanation and then connect it to the cause or final result of it. </br></br>  For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">He had a test on Monday. For this reason, he studied very hard on weekend. </span></br></br>  The connector <span class=\"strong\">however </span> makes a contrast between two opposite ideas that are connected. </br></br>  For example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">He studied very hard for the test, however, he forgot some information. </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Infinitives to Start Sentences and Gerunds as Nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We can start sentences using <strong>Infinitives</strong> and <strong>gerunds</strong>, they have different uses. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "So, to prioritize what application should get the attention of the processor, the operating system organizes information in a queue. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Organizing processes and prioritizing applications should get the attention of the processor first.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<strong>Infinitives</strong> are verbs with the preposition <strong>to</strong> at the beginning. We can use the <strong>infinitives</strong> to begin a sentence. Usually these sentences have two clauses. The first introducing the idea linked to the infinitive, and the second making an extension of the idea.<br/><br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\"><strong>To discard</strong> an item, the system always takes it from the head of the queue.</span><br/><br/>  In the case of <strong>gerunds</strong>, we can identify them because they finish with <strong>\u2013ing</strong>. In this case, the gerunds become a noun to express the idea that defines the verb.<br/><br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\"><strong>Programming</strong> is very difficult for some people.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talking about the concept of queue is not very difficult. I'm sure we'll get a good grade. However, if you want to practice, I will ask you some questions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Talking about the concept of queue is not very difficult.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Having those concepts clear helps a lot! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "List of Programming and Computer Science Terms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Let's take a look at some computer programming terminology", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>Abstract Base Class: In object-oriented programming, the base class from which other classes derive.   <li>Abstract Type: A nominative type system declared by a programmer.  <li>Acrobat: A document exchange software belonging to Adobe Systems which allows to convert documents into PDF.   <li>ActionScript: A scripting language similar to JavaScript.  <li>ActiveMovie: A multimedia streaming technology that allows users to watch multimedia content. </li> </ol>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "arranged ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be organized or placed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We just have to imagine a list of arranged items, and the organization of these items depends on their priority.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "carry out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make or perform an action or plan", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Computers often carry out different processes at the same time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prioritize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put in first place and give priority ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The operating system needs to prioritize to avoid delays or errors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "delay", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a postponement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The operating system needs to prioritize to avoid delays or errors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sum up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to express an idea briefly and concisely  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So, to sum up, I understood that a queue organizes different items by priority. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "buffering ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "referring to temporary storage  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's important to take into account concepts such as FIFO which means first in, first out; buffering which refers to storing data temporarily for later use.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Investigate about queues in software programming.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a list of examples of processes that involve queues.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the list with your class, remember to use statements using for this reason and however. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand what a queue in software programming is. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list examples of queues.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with my classmates.", "type": "text"}]}]}